---
const columns = [
  "Kampa",
  "ChatGPT free",
  "Jasper",
  "HubSpot Campaign Assistant",
];

const rows = [
  {
    label: "Complete 90-day campaign package",
    cells: [
      "yes",
      "blank prompt, you assemble",
      "assets only, no strategy",
      "landing page + email + ad copy only",
    ],
  },
  {
    label: "Plans within your budget & hours",
    cells: ["yes", "if you know to ask", "no", "no"],
  },
  {
    label: "Cost",
    cells: [
      "~€1/campaign (your API key)",
      "free but unstructured",
      "€59-69/mo",
      "free, but funnels to €20-890/mo",
    ],
  },
  {
    label: "Signup required",
    cells: ["none", "account", "account + card", "HubSpot account"],
  },
  {
    label: "Your data stored on their servers",
    cells: ["no — browser only", "yes", "yes", "yes"],
  },
  {
    label: "Export you own (md/PDF/ics)",
    cells: ["yes", "copy-paste", "limited", "limited"],
  },
];
---

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Comparison</p>
      <h2>Why not just ChatGPT?</h2>
      <p>Fair question. Here's the honest answer.</p>
    </div>

    {/* overflow-x wrapper is mandatory — the body must never scroll sideways */}
    <div
      class="overflow-x-auto"
      tabindex="0"
      role="region"
      aria-label="Comparison table"
    >
      <table class="compare">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Capability</th>
            {
              columns.map((name, i) => (
                <th scope="col" class:list={[i === 0 && "hi"]}>
                  {name}
                </th>
              ))
            }
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            rows.map((row) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{row.label}</th>
                {row.cells.map((cell, i) => (
                  <td class:list={[i === 0 && "hi"]}>{cell}</td>
                ))}
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 max-w-[680px] text-ink-soft">
      You could build this yourself in ChatGPT with the right 15 prompts. Kampa
      is those prompts, in the right order, with your constraints enforced and
      the output packaged. That's the whole product — and it's why it's free.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* One-per-file layout: the comparison table is not a shared pattern, so it
     lives here rather than in global.css. Values are contract §6.11. */
  table.compare {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 44rem;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  table.compare th,
  table.compare td {
    padding: 14px 16px;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  table.compare thead th {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-mono-label);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-th);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  table.compare tbody th {
    width: 34%;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  /* the Kampa column */
  table.compare .hi {
    background-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--coral) 6%, transparent);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  table.compare thead th.hi {
    background-image: var(--grad);
    background-size: 100% 2px;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    background-position: top left;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    table.compare {
      font-size: var(--text-xs);
      min-width: 38rem;
    }
    table.compare th,
    table.compare td {
      padding: 12px 12px;
    }
  }
</style>
